# RoboCarl (AI brief)

AI-only context. Prefer this over re-exploring. **Update this rule** when levels, systems, or folder layout change.

## Game
2D URP portrait puzzle. Playfield **9×19.5** (`AspectRatioCamera`). Player does **not** control Carl — Carl auto-walks to LOS-visible oil/battery pickups; player **drags metal walls**. Energy drains ~25s; oil drains with walk. Energy 0 → lose. WinLine → MainMenu.

## Levels
| Level | Load path | Content |
|------:|-----------|---------|
| 1 | `LevelSession=1` → `SampleScene` | Floors, Spring, WinLine, Carl, `DefaultLevelSpawns` (oil+battery) |
| 2 | `LevelSession=2` → **same** `SampleScene` | `Level2Layout.Apply()` strips Spring/WinLine/FloorRight; full Floor; `Level2Spawns` (2 batteries + vertical `DraggableWall`) |

- Menu: `MainMenuController` — levels 1–2 only; Play Mode starts on `MainMenu` (`PlayModeStartScene`).
- **`Level2.unity` is unused** by the menu (build entry may exist). Do not assume it is the L2 runtime path.
- Spawns: `LevelSpawnConfig` SO → pickups + walls. Assets: `Resources/DefaultLevelSpawns`, `Resources/Level2Spawns`.

## Script map (`Assets/Scripts/`)
- `CarlResources` — energy/oil; spawn pickups; game over
- `CarlLocomotion` — walk, ground, step-up, spring launch
- `CarlPickupChaser` — closest **clear LOS** pickup (raycast; Debug.DrawLine green/red)
- `CarlVisual` / `CarlSparkEffect` — `CarlAppearance` sprites; sparks if oil low
- `GameDirector` — L2 layout hook; WinLine ensure; spawn walls
- `LevelSession` / `Level2Layout` — selected level + L2 scene rewrite
- `ResourcePickup` — kinematic trigger oil/battery (procedural quads)
- `SpringPad` — compress → `LaunchVertical(7.7)`
- `WinLine` — green goal → MainMenu
- `DraggableWall` — drag along length; `dragPositive`/`dragNegative` from start; `Pointer.current`
- `MainMenuController` / `MenuUi` — runtime UI (Levels/Rules/Settings)
- `LoseOverlay` — restart = **active scene name** (keeps L2 via `LevelSession`)
- `GameSprites` / `SpriteQuad` — white quad props (never null material → magenta)
- `GameMusic` / `GameSfx` / `GameAudioSettings` — BGM + one-shots from `Resources/Audio/`

## Visuals
- **Procedural:** floors, spring, wall, pickups, win line, most UI chrome → `GameSprites.White`
- **PNGs:** `Art/Carl/*` via `Resources/CarlAppearance.asset`; icons `Resources/UI/`
- Rules panel documents objects (Carl states, pickups, Spring, WinLine, Draggable Wall)

## Conventions for agents
- Input System **only** (`activeInputHandler: 1`) — no legacy `Input.*` for gameplay
- New interactables: self-build visual in code + Rules entry + spawn/config if level-driven
- Prefer extending `LevelSpawnConfig` / Resources assets over hand-editing huge `.unity` YAML
- **Do not regenerate/randomize `.meta` GUIDs** — many are hand-assigned; breaks SO/scene refs
- `*.png` / `*.wav` are **normal Git blobs** (not LFS). Other media types may still be LFS in `.gitattributes`

## Layout
```
Assets/Art/           source PNGs
Assets/Resources/     runtime Loads (Audio, UI, *Spawns, CarlAppearance)
Assets/Scripts/       gameplay (+ Data/)
Assets/Scenes/        MainMenu, SampleScene (L1+L2 base), Level2 (unused)
Assets/Editor/        PlayModeStartScene
Assets/Settings/      URP
```
